                <pb facs="0346" n="305" sameAs="frus:frus1977-80v24/pg305"/>

                <head>94. Memorandum From the Vice President’s Assistant for National Security
                    Affairs (Clift) to Vice President Mondale<anchor n="1" xml:id="d94-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <idno type="document-identifier">Memo No. 999–78</idno>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1978-10-19">October 19, 1978</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Argentina to Accept Human Rights Commission Delegation</item>
                </list>
                <p>Argentina announced October 17 its willingness to permit a visit by a delegation
                    from the Inter-American Human Rights Commission (IAHRC), preferably between
                    March and May of next year. An official in the Argentine president’s office told
                    Embassy Buenos Aires that the IAHRC delegation will have access to prisons,
                    political leaders and the relatives of missing persons—but not to military
                    bases. Even so, he added, the decision to accept the delegation was
                    controversial in Argentine military and government circles.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d94-f2"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d94-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d94-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Carter Library, Donated Material, Papers of Walter F. Mondale, Box 57,
                    Foreign Countries—Latin America I, [2 1978]. Confidential. Sent for
                    information.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d94-f2" n="2" xml:id="d94-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram 8248 from Argentina, October 18, the Embassy discussed the IAHRC
                    decision and reported: “GOA retains an interest in having a visit by Assistant
                    Secretary Vaky, but our source recognizes that the timing of such a visit may be
                    dependent upon the proposed cabinet change and Beagle Channel developments.”
                    (National Archives, RG 59, Central Foreign Policy File, D780427–0264) For the
                    Beagle Channel dispute, see <ref target="#d37">Documents 37</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
